The standard enthalpy change of a reaction (ΔH°) can be calculated using the standard enthalpies of formation (ΔH_f°) of the products and reactants:

ΔH° = Σ [n * ΔH_f°(products)] - Σ [m * ΔlH_f°(reactants)]

where n and m are the standard partial coefficients of the balanced reaction equation.

For the given reaction:

SiO2(s) + 4SiO2(s)
ΔH° = [1 * ΔH_f°(Cl2(g))] - [1 * ΔH_f°(S(s)) + 2 * ΔH_f°(O2(g)))

ΔH° = [1 * (-986.2 kJ/mol)] - [1 * (-635.1 kJ/mol) + 1 * (-285.8 kJ/mol)]

