ΔHCl2(s) = -986.2 kJ/mol + 635.1 kJ/mol + 285.8 kJ/mol

ΔH° = -986.2 + 635.1 + 285.8

ΔH° = -65.3 kJ/mol

The standard enthalpy change for the reaction of carbon with oxygen to form water is -65.3 kJ/mol.
