The compound [Pt(NH₃)₄C₁₂]²⁺ is a complex ion, but the two C₁₂ ions are ions. Therefore, for.
\[[P.(NH₃)₄C₂]C₂ \rightarrow [P.(NH₃)₄C₂]²⁺ + 2c⁻\]

Thus, two charge ions are produced for C₁₂ that is displaced from the complex. Therefore, the number of charge ions produced is 2.
