","(a) **Temperature after 5 minutes**:  
   
   
   Using the thermal conductivity, heat capacity, mass, and surface area, we can calculate the temperature of the material after 5 minutes using the following equation:
   \[
   T(t) = T_\infty + (T_0 - T_\infty) \exp\left(-\frac{t}{R_th}\right)
   \]
   where \( T(t) \) is the temperature at time \( t \), \( T_\infty \) is the ambient temperature, \( T_0 \) is the initial temperature, \( t \) is the time, and \( R_{th} \) is the thermal resistance.  
   \[
   R_{th} = \frac{m c_p}{h A} = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{56.8 \times 0.075} = 10.5 \text{ K/m}^2
   \]
   Substituting the values:
   \[
   T(5 \text{ min}) = 20 + (345 - 20) \exp\left(-\frac{5 \times 60}{10.5}\right) = 20 + 325 \exp(-28.57) = 20 + 325 \times 1.0 \times 10^{-12} = 20.000325 \text{°C}
   \]
   The temperature after 5 minutes is approximately 20°C.

