","The magnetic field strength (B) at the center of a circular loop of wire is given by the formula:

B = (μ₀ * N * I) / (2 * r)

where:
- μ₀ is the permeability of free space (4π × 10⁻⁷ Tm/A)
- N is the number of turns in the coil
- I is the current between the wire (in amperes)
- r is the radius of the coil (in meters)

Plugging in the given values:

B = (4π × 10⁻⁷ Tm/A * 100 * 1 A) / (2 * 0.2 m)

B = (4π × 10⁻⁷ * 100) / 0.4

B ≈ (1.2566 × 10⁻⁴) / 0.4

B ≈ 3.14 × 10⁻⁵ T

So, the magnetic field strength at the center of the coil is approximately 3.14 × 10⁻⁵ Tesla.",fluency,"# Task Description
